sc = F.get("score", {}); sc_txt = "; ".join(f"{k} (n {v['n']}): " + (best(v) if "p_family" in v else "too few to test") for k, v in sc.items())
ROWS = f"""| 2026-11-12 | E1 release-time detection | {len(T)} statement days 2011-01-26 → 2026-10-28; from 2013 the note's largest 5-minute move falls at 14:00 on {share14:.0%} of days, at 14:15 or 12:30 on the rest — on quiet days the largest of three small moves is arbitrary, so the detected time is noisy. | the detection rule is imperfect; amendment below fixes 14:00 from March 2013 | **#139 {'right' if p139 else 'wrong (counted)'}** |
| 2026-11-12 | E1(a) when the move happens (signed by the note's whole-day direction) | gold: whole day {g['day']:+.1f} bp (n {g['n']}) = before the release {g['pre']:+.1f} + first 5 minutes {g['f5']:+.1f} + minutes 5–30 {g['m5_30']:+.1f} + 30 minutes after → close {g['rest']:+.1f}. So {g['pre'] / g['day']:.0%} is in before the release, {g['f5'] / g['day']:.0%} in the first five minutes, and {(g['m5_30'] + g['rest']) / g['day']:.0%} after the first five minutes. The 10-year note itself: {F['decomposition']['ZN']['day']:+.1f} = {F['decomposition']['ZN']['pre']:+.1f} + {F['decomposition']['ZN']['f5']:+.1f} + {F['decomposition']['ZN']['m5_30']:+.1f} + {F['decomposition']['ZN']['rest']:+.1f}. | The day's link is spread over the whole day; most of it comes AFTER the release, and the largest piece after 14:30, when the Chair's press conference brings new information. Caution: this cut is signed by where the note ended the day, which is not known at the release. | **#136 {'right' if p136 else 'wrong (counted)'}** — predicted over half in the first 30 minutes and under 20% later; found {first30:.0%} and {rest:.0%} |
| 2026-11-12 | E1(b) **primary: gold, entering after the release in the direction of the note's first minutes** | best cell {best(gc)}; placebo days mean {gc['placebo'].get('mean', float('nan')):+.1f} bp. S&P: {best(F['catch']['ES'])}. Nasdaq: {best(F['catch']['NQ'])}. Note: {best(F['catch']['ZN'])}. | **Gold is NOT a grade A candidate** on this rule: the note's first minutes do not tell which way gold (or anything else) goes for the rest of the day. The gold–Fed finding stays SUBJECTIVE grade B. What (a) adds: the move is not over at the release, so a reader of the statement and press conference could in principle still act — but following the first minutes is not the way. | **#137 {'right' if p137 else 'wrong (counted)'}** |
| 2026-11-12 | E1(c) signed by the statement's own score, Nasdaq future | {sc_txt} | Large in size, not established (secondary bar p < 0.005; these are above 0.05 too) and only the 45 statements that had been scored. Hindsight in the reader cannot be excluded. Follow-up registered below: score all statements. | — |
| 2026-11-12 | E2 the 08:30 releases ({R['continuation']['ES']['n_days']} days) | first 5 minutes agree in sign with the composition score on {agree:.0%} of days. Continuation — S&P: {best(R['continuation']['ES'])}; Nasdaq: {best(R['continuation']['NQ'])}. Score — S&P: {best(R['score']['ES'])}; Nasdaq: {best(R['score']['NQ'])}. First move against the score ({R['score_disagrees']['NQ']['n_days']} days) — S&P: {best(R['score_disagrees']['ES'])}; Nasdaq: {best(R['score_disagrees']['NQ'])}. | No secondary family reaches p < 0.005. Closest: when the first five minutes went against what the document's composition says, the Nasdaq future moved toward the document over the next hour (p 0.017) — a candidate for a larger sample, not a finding. The first move neither continues nor reverses reliably. | **#138 {'right' if p138 else 'wrong (counted)'}** |
| 2026-11-12 | **Amendment registered before running — v3e-2** | (1) **Release time by schedule:** from March 2013 the statement time is fixed at 14:00 (the published schedule); earlier days keep the note-dated rule. E1 is rerun whole (`fed --schedule`); the first run stays on record beside it. (2) **Every statement scored:** the same reader, prompt and cache (n1-doc-v3) applied to all statements in the corpus, so E1(c) runs on about 130 days instead of 45 (≈ US$1–2; `score`). Verdict rule unchanged. Priors: **#140** with the fixed time gold is still not a grade A candidate (family p ≥ 0.05). **#141** with every statement scored, the Nasdaq rule signed by the score does not reach family p < 0.05 on all statement days — the +45 bp shrinks by more than half. | — | — |
"""
